## WHATWG Encoding Standard — `index-*.txt` normative index tables

`src/testdata/index-windows-1250.txt`, `index-windows-1252.txt`,
`index-iso-8859-2.txt`, and `index-iso-8859-15.txt` are vendored verbatim from
the Encoding Standard published at https://encoding.spec.whatwg.org/, each
file's own header carrying `Date: 2024-09-18` (the version fetched). Each is
the normative byte-0x80..0xFF -> codepoint mapping for that code page. Driven
mechanically by `src/normative_vectors.zig` (parser) and `src/normative_test.zig`
(the exhaustive 128-entry-per-page cross-check against `root.zig`'s tables).

The Encoding Standard's own terms (`LICENSE` in the `whatwg/encoding`
repository):

