CC-BY 4.0 in full: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode
(the licence is not reproduced here — it is ~7 000 words and, unlike the BSD
and MIT texts elsewhere in this file, it requires a URI rather than a copy:
§3(a)(1)(C) is satisfied by "a URI or hyperlink to this Public License").

INDICATION OF MODIFICATIONS, per CC-BY 4.0 §3(a)(1)(B): none. The four
`index-*.txt` files are vendored byte-for-byte as published, headers included.
Nothing was reformatted, filtered or re-encoded — which is also why the
`Date:` line in each file's own header is the version pin cited above.

## Unicode.org — `8859-1.TXT`

`src/testdata/8859-1.TXT` is vendored verbatim from
https://www.unicode.org/Public/MAPPINGS/ISO8859/8859-1.TXT (table version 2.0,
dated 1999-07-27, header last updated 2015-12-02): the normative ISO/IEC
8859-1:1998 -> Unicode mapping. WHATWG does not publish a separate index table
for this page — in the WHATWG algorithm the *label* "iso-8859-1" is an alias
for the windows-1252 *encoding*, but this module's `iso_8859_1` is the true,
distinct ISO/IEC 8859-1 code page (pure Latin-1 identity high half), so
Unicode.org is the correct normative source here instead. Driven by the same
`normative_vectors.zig` / `normative_test.zig` pair (a second parser, since the
column layout differs from the WHATWG files).

